---
description: Deploy any Dockerized website (zip + Dockerfile/docker-compose) on Windows, macOS or Linux
globs: ["**/*"]
alwaysApply: true
---

When the user asks to run, deploy, or troubleshoot a Docker website project:

1. Read `AGENTS.md` in this repository and follow its workflow.
2. Start with `python scripts/deploy.py check`; do not assume Docker/WSL are ready.
3. Ask before installing software, changing system settings, or stopping processes.
4. Extract with `python scripts/deploy.py extract "<zip>"`; never overwrite an existing directory.
5. Inspect with `python scripts/deploy.py inspect "<project_root>"` to get services and host port.
6. Start with `docker compose up -d --build` inside the project root.
7. Verify with `python scripts/deploy.py verify --url "http://localhost:<port>"`.
8. On failure, read `references/troubleshooting.md` and match the error text.

Never modify the project source. Never expose the service publicly without explicit consent.
